# A Luxel library scene — Apache-2.0. Grammar: library/README.md.
# No pattern at all: classic C9 bulbs. `bulb-string` is a 32x12 tile of two
# sagging strings whose two frames trade which half of the bulbs glows; tiled
# over the whole panel it is a curtain of lights. The box is an explicit 64x63
# (since #985 a zero `w`/`h` under `tile` would mean the whole layout too), so
# on a 32x32 it simply clips to the panel. A strip wants a 1-row variant of the
# sprite (the planned strip-bulbs scene): this one shows only its top row there.
S - Bulb String
L color 0 0 0 0 normal 100 none fill 1
N Night
K 06040a
L sprite 0 1 64 63 normal 100 none tile 1
N Bulbs
I @spr/bulb-string
